# NASBot Configuration Template
# Copy to nasbot.config.local and customize for your environment, then pass it with
#   ./scripts/package_runtime.sh --config nasbot.config.local
#
# IMPORTANT
#   * --config re-runs the whole hierarchy WHILE it is parsed, so it overrides any
#     flag given before it. Put --config first, flags after.
#   * Without --config this file is auto-loaded by scripts/common.sh and then
#     discarded for the keys the scripts re-initialise from the environment
#     (BUILD_ARCH, PACKAGE_OUT_DIR, VERSION, BINARY_NAME, INCLUDE_*,
#     ADDITIONAL_FILES). Environment variables (NASBOT_*) are the reliable way to
#     override those.
#   * Only the keys below are read by a script. Keys that used to be listed here
#     (GO_VERSION, BUILD_FLAGS, DEPLOY_USER/HOST, USE_RSYNC, WATCHDOG_*,
#     UPDATE_CHECK_INTERVAL, RESTART_SCRIPT, AUTO_APPLY_RELEASES, CACHE_DIR,
#     PARALLEL_WORKERS, NOTIFICATIONS_*, HEALTH_CHECK_*, NETWORK_INTERFACE,
#     CUSTOM_ENV, LOG_BACKUP_COUNT, TZ, UMASK) were never read and have been removed.
#     Watchdog and update behaviour is configured in the bot's config.json
#     (fs_watchdog and update sections), not here.
#
# Format: plain KEY="value" lines. load_config greps for '^\s*[A-Z_]+=' and sources
# the result, so anything else is ignored silently.

# ============================================================================
# BUILD SETTINGS (package_runtime.sh, deploy_runtime_rsync.sh)
# ============================================================================
# Valid architectures: native, arm64, amd64, armv7, 386
BUILD_ARCH="native"
# Version string stamped into the binary with -ldflags -X main.Version=...
VERSION="dev"

# ============================================================================
# DEPLOYMENT SETTINGS (deploy_runtime_rsync.sh)
# ============================================================================
# Default deployment target. --target is required unless this key is set AND the
# file is re-loaded with --config. Format: user@host:/absolute/path
DEPLOY_TARGET=""
# Extra rsync options, split on whitespace
RSYNC_OPTS="--compress --progress"
# Colon-separated names that --delete never removes
RSYNC_EXCLUDE_DELETE="config.json:nasbot.log:nasbot.pid:nasbot_state.json:#recycle"

# ============================================================================
# PACKAGE SETTINGS (package_runtime.sh)
# ============================================================================
# Output directory for the packaged runtime (script default: ./dist/runtime)
PACKAGE_OUT_DIR="./dist/runtime"
# Include config.example.json in the bundle
INCLUDE_EXAMPLE_CONFIG="true"
# Include README_RUNTIME.md in the bundle
INCLUDE_README_RUNTIME="true"
# Additional files to include (colon-separated paths relative to repo root)
ADDITIONAL_FILES=""
# Binary file name (without extension)
BINARY_NAME="nasbot"

# ============================================================================
# LOGGING
# ============================================================================
# [DEBUG] lines for every resolved key
VERBOSE="false"

# ============================================================================
# THE BUNDLE RUNNER READS ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES, NOT THIS FILE
# ============================================================================
# On the NAS, start_bot.sh (= scripts/start_bot_runtime.sh) sources common.sh with
# NASBOT_NO_AUTO_LOAD=1, so none of the keys above reach it. Pass these inline:
#
#   NASBOT_LOG_FILE=/var/log/nasbot/app.log
#   NASBOT_PID_FILE=/run/nasbot.pid
#   NASBOT_STATE_FILE=/var/lib/nasbot/state.json
#   NASBOT_LOG_MAX_SIZE_MB=50
#   NASBOT_AUTO_RESTART_ON_UPDATE=true
#   NASBOT_UPDATE_FILE_PATTERN="nasbot-update*"
#   NASBOT_ULIMIT_N=4096
#   NASBOT_VERBOSE=true
#   NASBOT_DEBUG=true
#   ./start_bot.sh start
